      ⍝!MODES (B)
      ⍝ WRITE, in (B) only: an exercise with its functions hidden, and its
      ⍝ value; the reader writes the expression, which is run with execute
      ⍝ and marked. The value itself and an empty line are refused; right
      ⍝ expressions, wrong ones, three wrong in a row revealing the
      ⍝ exercise, then an expression that is an error, which stops WRITE
      ⍝ with its report; a bare branch clears it, and WRITE is stopped at
      ⍝ the topic prompt. The file's latent expression prints DESCRIBE on
      ⍝ load.
      )LOAD 2 DRILL
DRILL -- EXERCISES IN APL, MADE AT RANDOM AND MARKED.

   EASY        ONE FUNCTION ON SINGLE NUMBERS.
   DRILL       ONE OR TWO FUNCTIONS ON VECTORS.
   HARD        TWO FUNCTIONS, PARENTHESES, REDUCTIONS.
   WRITE       AN EXERCISE WITH ITS FUNCTIONS HIDDEN: WRITE IT.
   SHOW N      PRINT N EXERCISES, EACH WITH ITS ANSWER.

EACH ASKS WHICH FUNCTIONS TO DRILL, THEN PRINTS AN EXERCISE
AND A QUAD PROMPT. TYPE THE ANSWER AS APL: A NUMBER, OR A
VECTOR, OR AN EXPRESSION THAT MAKES ONE. STOP ENDS THE DRILL
AND PRINTS THE SCORE. HOWDRILL SAYS MORE.
